        <h3 id="isa-annexure-1">Annexure 1: CCC Integration</h3>
        <h4 id="isa-a1"><span>1.</span>Purpose</h4>
        <p>This Agreement outlines the terms and conditions under which ClearTax will provide integration services for connecting the Customer's ERP system with Clear Compliance Cloud using the Clear GL Stream Add-on.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a2"><span>2.</span>Scope of Work</h4>
        <h4 id="isa-a2-1"><span>2.1</span>Inclusions</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span>Installation and configuration of the Clear GL Stream Add-on in the Customer's ERP environment.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span>Automated data extraction from ERP, secure uploading to Clear Compliance Cloud, and data transformation for GST Sale Register, GST Purchase Register, General Ledger.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>3.</span>Documentation and one-time training sessions for the Customer's functional team.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>4.</span>Hypercare support for one month following integration.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a2-2"><span>2.2</span>Exclusions</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span>Any customization or maintenance of the Customer's ERP system beyond what is necessary for the integration.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span>Configuration and maintenance at the infrastructure level, including network or firewall settings.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>3.</span>Real-time data synchronization</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>4.</span>On-site support services.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a3"><span>3.</span>Customer Responsibilities</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span>Provide the necessary access to ERP systems, including remote access and VPN credentials.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span>Complete all prerequisites, including whitelisting API hostnames and enabling required network configurations.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>3.</span>Provide sample data for testing and data confirmation, along with confirmation of test results.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>4.</span>Appoint a project leader and provide a SWAT team for collaboration during the integration process.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4"><span>4.</span>Project Stages and Timelines</h4>
        <p>The integration project will follow a structured life cycle with the following stages and timelines:</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-1"><span>4.1</span>Plan Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Pre-kick-off Meeting</strong>: ClearTax and the Customer will set up a kick-off meeting within three (3) days from the Integration Asset Start Date (as set out in the Order Form) to understand the Customer's IT environment, introduce key stakeholders, and discuss the integration development project.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span><strong>Prerequisites Closure</strong>: The Customer shall provide access to ClearTax's information technology systems, including developer provisioning and establishing network connectivity, within twenty-one (21) days from the kick-off meeting. This stage ensures that all activities to start the project are completed.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>3.</span><strong>Kick-off Meeting</strong>: Formally introduce the teams, share the project plan, and ensure that all prerequisites are completed. The kick-off meeting will set realistic expectations for baselines such as milestone schedules and project schedules.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-2"><span>4.2</span>Design Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Requirements Gathering</strong>: Update query configurations and initiate the data extraction process. Conduct workshops to clarify requirements.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-3"><span>4.3</span>Develop Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Development</strong>: Replicate base models, initiate development, and perform testing for specific changes and functionalities. ClearTax will implement the integration development as per the agreed integration development plan within thirty-five (35) days of completing the prerequisites.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span><strong>Data Reconciliation</strong>: End-to-end testing from ERP to Clear and reconciliation. Integration development will be delivered to the Customer for data confirmation upon completion.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-4"><span>4.4</span>Test Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Data Confirmation</strong>: Validate the transformed data with the Customer and get sign-off on the go-live. The Customer shall complete the data confirmation within twenty-one (21) days and notify ClearTax of its acceptance or any issues.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-5"><span>4.5</span>Deploy Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Cutover Activities</strong>: Execute final tasks, validate transformation, and perform smoke tests for production environments. ClearTax will move the integration to the production environment within ten (10) days of receiving the data confirmation sign-off.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a4-6"><span>4.6</span>Close Stage</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span><strong>Hyper Care Support</strong>: Provide one month of post-go-live support to address any issues related to the integration within the initially agreed-upon scope.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span><strong>Annual Maintenance Contract (AMC)</strong>: Not included in the standard integration package. All changes post-go-live will be handled as Change Requests.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a5"><span>5.</span>Timelines and Grace Period</h4>
        <p>The Parties hereby agree that the integration process shall in no event exceed ninety (90) days including grace period. A maximum of thirty (30) days grace period may be allowed to both Parties for delays in meeting the deliverables provided herein.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a6"><span>6.</span>Acceptance Criteria</h4>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span>The integration will be considered successful and accepted by the Customer when the following conditions are met:</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>(a)</span>Seamless connectivity between ERP and Clear Compliance Cloud.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>(b)</span>Successful data transfer, transformation, and ingestion of sales and purchase documents.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>(c)</span>Completion of data confirmation with all issues resolved to the satisfaction of both Parties.</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>(d)</span>Confirmation from the Customer within 14 calendar days of handing over for data completion.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a7"><span>7.</span>Change Management</h4>
        <p>Any changes to the initially agreed-upon scope must be formally requested and approved by both Parties. Changes may affect project timelines and costs.</p>
        <p><span>7.1</span>Enhancement of Scope of Services: Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, the Customer agrees that any request for integration development which is not stipulated in the Order Form shall be considered as a request for enhancement of the scope of Services and may be provided by ClearTax, at its sole and absolute discretion, and at such additional cost as notified by ClearTax.</p>
        <p><span>7.2</span>Post-Delivery ChangesAny request for changes post-delivery of the integration development must be in writing and shall set out in sufficient detail that the change requested is within the scope of Services set out in the Order Form and is in accordance with the agreed integration development plan. ClearTax shall then use commercially reasonable efforts to perform the changes requested to the extent feasible in ClearTax’s sole discretion and reissue the integration development to the Customer.</p>
        <p><span>7.3</span>Additional Costs for Changes Post-Acceptance: The Customer shall be liable to make the entire payment as per the Integration Asset Start Date as set out in the Order Form. Any changes subsequent to acceptance of the integration development requested by the Customer, or if the scope of Services is not completed within the relevant time period set out above (including the grace period), may be carried out at the request of the Customer by ClearTax at its sole and absolute discretion, and at such additional cost as may be notified by ClearTax.</p>
        <h4 id="isa-a8"><span>8.</span>No Refund or Waiver of Payment Obligations</h4>
        <p>Notwithstanding anything contained in this Agreement, under no circumstance shall the Customer claim for a refund of any charges (including one-time charges under the Order Form) or seek a waiver of its payment obligations on account of the Customer’s delay (whether due to inactivity or otherwise) or failure to undertake the following within the relevant timelines set out above (including the grace period):</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>1.</span>Providing access to its information technology systems, including developer provisioning and establishing network connectivity, past data for reconciliation, or failure to confirm and finalize all other requirements, if any, as may be required by ClearTax for integration development;</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>2.</span>Verifying data and confirming acceptance of the integration development post handing over for data confirmation;</p>
        <p class="pl-6"><span>3.</span>Notifying ClearTax of the issues or bugs in the integration development.</p>
